### Normalized scores (1–100)

- **Tool use: 80/100.** Routes to strong underlying models (DeepSeek V4.1, Kimi) with tool-calling capabilities. Capped by routing variability and absent direct benchmarks.
- **Reasoning: 80/100.** Inherits reasoning from frontier models. Intelligent routing may select optimal model per task. Capped by inconsistent behavior and absent GPQA/HLE data.
- **Context window: 85/100.** Underlying models support up to 1M tokens. Capped by uncertainty on actual routing limits.
- **Multimodal: 65/100.** Vision capability may be available depending on routed model; inconsistent. Capped by routing-dependent modality support.
- **Coding: 82/100.** Routes to DeepSeek V4.1 and Kimi — both strong coding models. Capped by absent direct SWE-bench/LiveCodeBench data.
- **Cost efficiency: 95/100.** Free/trial pricing during feedback phase. Exceptional value while available. Capped by uncertain long-term pricing.
- **Overall Score: 78/100.** Mean of (80 + 80 + 85 + 65 + 82) / 5 = 78.4, rounded to 78. Promising routing approach inheriting strong model capabilities, limited by inconsistency and opacity.

